<% content_for :title, "Enforcers and Responders | SafeSpace Malaysia" %>

<section class="page-hero page-hero--blue">
  <div class="container page-hero__content">
    <span class="eyebrow">For first responders and supporters</span>
    <h1>Enforcers and support agencies</h1>
    <p>A calm, respectful first response can help a survivor feel believed and regain control over what happens next.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="agencies">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Who does what</span><h2>Agencies involved in protection</h2><p>Different organisations have different responsibilities. The directory below helps users identify the appropriate service.</p></div>
    <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Agency roles, scroll horizontally on small screens">
      <table class="agency-table">
        <caption>Malaysian enforcement agencies and support services</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Agency or service</th><th scope="col">Main role</th><th scope="col">When to approach</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Royal Malaysia Police (PDRM)</th><td>Receive reports, investigate offences and help enforce protection orders.</td><td>Reporting violence or seeking urgent police help.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Social Welfare Department (JKM)</th><td>Authorised officers issue EPOs and assist with protection and welfare referrals.</td><td>Emergency protection or welfare assistance.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Malaysian courts</th><td>Issue Interim Protection Orders and Protection Orders.</td><td>Applications for court protection with agency assistance.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Hospital One Stop Crisis Centre</th><td>Provide medical treatment, document injuries and coordinate referrals.</td><td>Injuries or medical attention after violence.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Women's Aid Organisation (WAO)</th><td>Offer survivor support, safety planning and shelter referrals. WAO is an NGO, not an enforcement agency.</td><td>Confidential support and help understanding options.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="source-links">Sources: <a href="https://www.jkm.gov.my/portalassets/jkm/documents/garis-panduan-pengendalian-kes-keganasan-rumah-tangga.pdf">KPWKM / JKM case guidelines</a> and <a href="https://wao.org.my/what-to-expect-when-you-contact-wao/">WAO service information</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading section-heading--center">
      <span class="eyebrow">A survivor-centred approach</span>
      <h2>Listen. Believe. Support.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="response-grid">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Check immediate safety</h3><p>Ask whether they need urgent medical help or are in immediate danger. Call 999 when emergency intervention is needed.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Listen without judgement</h3><p>Let them share at their own pace. Avoid interrupting, investigating or asking why they did not leave sooner.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Affirm and believe</h3><p>Say clearly that the violence is not their fault and that they deserve support.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Explain available options</h3><p>Offer accurate information about medical care, specialist services and reporting without promising an outcome.</p></article>
      <article><span>05</span><h3>Respect their decisions</h3><p>Do not pressure them to report, confront the person causing harm or take a step they are not ready to take.</p></article>
      <article><span>06</span><h3>Protect confidentiality</h3><p>Share information only with consent, except where your role or the law requires action. Explain any limits clearly.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint">
  <div class="container say-grid">
    <div class="say-card say-card--do">
      <span class="say-card__label">Helpful language</span>
      <ul>
        <li>“I believe you.”</li>
        <li>“This is not your fault.”</li>
        <li>“What would help you feel safer right now?”</li>
        <li>“Would you like me to explain some options?”</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="say-card say-card--avoid">
      <span class="say-card__label">Language to avoid</span>
      <ul>
        <li>“Why didn't you leave?”</li>
        <li>“Are you sure that happened?”</li>
        <li>“You have to report this.”</li>
        <li>“I know exactly how you feel.”</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--compact">
  <div class="container action-banner action-banner--blue">
    <div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Make a warm referral</span><h2>Connect, do not simply redirect.</h2><p>With consent, help the survivor contact a suitable service and confirm what will happen next.</p></div>
    <%= link_to "View support directory", hotline_path, class: "button button--light" %>
  </div>
</section>
